# Code Quality

- Remove dead code and unreachable branches.

- Avoid redundant conditions.

- Document non-obvious:
  - design decisions
  - tradeoffs
  - safety constraints
  - unusual implementation choices

- Do not write comments that only repeat what the code does.

- Document limitations of heuristics and static analysis.

- Temporary placeholders are acceptable only if they can later become configurable.

- Prefer reusable capabilities over isolated patches.
